    "shortDescription":  "Submit a URL, get back a build-ready Android, iOS, PWA, Electron or Capacitor project. Your signing keys never leave your machine.",
    "longDescription":  "Submit a URL. The AmberOne API scans it for wrap compatibility, applies the fixes it safely can to the\ngenerated package, and returns a downloadable project you build yourself.\n\n**What you get is a project, not a compiled app.** Android and iOS outputs are Capacitor\nprojects ready for `gradlew assembleRelease` or Xcode\u0027s Archive — which also means your signing\nkeys never leave your machine. Nothing is compiled, signed, installed, or submitted on your behalf.\n\nEvery response uses the same envelope: `{ ok: true, data, requestId }` or\n`{ ok: false, error: { code, message }, requestId }`. Branch on `ok`; match on `error.code`,\nwhich is stable. Quote `requestId` in any support request.",
    "endpointCount":  9,
    "authentication":  "Bearer token (also accepts X-API-Key)",
    "sandbox":  "Keys prefixed wrap_test_ run the full pipeline and are never billed.",
